gged, no false positives |\\\\n    14→| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\\\\n    15→\\\\n    16→**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\\\\n    17→\\\\n    18→---\\\\n    19→\\\\n    20→## Category Details\\\\n    21→\\\\n    22→### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\\\\n    23→\\\\n    24→**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\\\\n    25→\\\\n    26→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n    27→|-------|----------|\\\\n    28→| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\\\\n    29→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\\\\n    30→| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\\\\n    31→| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\\\\n    32→| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\\\\n    33→| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\\\\n    34→\\\\n    35→**Checklist:**\\\\n    36→- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\\\\n    37→- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\\\\n    38→- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\\\\n    39→- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\\\\n    40→- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\\\\n    41→- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\\\\n    42→- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\\\\n    43→- [ ] \\\\\\\"Chapter\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"Book\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"Part\\\\\\\" hierarchy correct\\\\n    44→\\\\n    45→---\\\\n    46→\\\\n    47→### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\\\\n    48→\\\\n    49→**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\\\\n    50→\\\\n    51→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n    52→|-------|----------|\\\\n    53→| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\\\\n    54→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\\\\n    55→| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\\\\n    56→| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\\\\n    57→| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\\\\n    58→| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\\\\n    59→\\\\n    60→**Checklist:**\\\\n    61→- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\\\\n    62→- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\\\\n    63→- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\\\\n    64→- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\\\\n    65→- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\\\\n    66→- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\\\\n    67→- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\\\\n    68→- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\\\\n    69→\\\\n    70→**Common Issues:**\\\\n    71→- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\\\\n    72→- Full names and nicknames not linked\\\\n    73→- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\\\\n    74→- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\\\\n    75→\\\\n    76→---\\\\n    77→\\\\n    78→### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\\\\n    79→\\\\n    80→**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\\\\n    81→\\\\n    82→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n    83→|-------|----------|\\\\n    84→| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\\\\n    85→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\\\\n    86→| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\\\\n    87→| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\\\\n    88→| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\\\\n    89→| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\\\\n    90→\\\\n    91→**Checklist:**\\\\n    92→- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\\\\n    93→- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\\\\n    94→- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\\\\n    95→- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\\\\n    96→- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\\\\n    97→- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\\\\n    98→\\\\n    99→---\\\\n   100→\\\\n   101→### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\\\\n   102→\\\\n   103→**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\\\\n   104→\\\\n   105→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n   106→|-------|----------|\\\\n   107→| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\\\\n   108→| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\\\\n   109→| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\\\\n   110→| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\\\\n   111→| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\\\\n   112→| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\\\\n   113→\\\\n   114→**Checklist:**\\\\n   115→- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\\\\n   116→- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\\\\n   117→- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\\\\n   118→- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\\\\n   119→- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\\\\n   120→- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\\\\n   121→- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\\\\n   122→\\\\n   123→---\\\\n   124→\\\\n   125→### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\\\\n   126→\\\\n   127→**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\\\\n   128→\\\\n   129→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n   130→|-------|----------|\\\\n   131→| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\\\\n   132→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\\\\n   133→| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\\\\n   134→| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\\\\n   135→| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\\\\n   136→| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\\\\n   137→\\\\n   138→**Checklist:**\\\\n   139→- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\\\\n   140→- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\\\\n   141→- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\\\\n   142→- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\\\\n   143→- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\\\\n   144→- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\\\\n   145→- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\\\\n   146→\\\\n   147→---\\\\n   148→\\\\n   149→### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\\\\n   150→\\\\n   151→**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\\\\n   152→\\\\n   153→| Score | Criteria |\\\\n   154→|-------|----------|\\\\n   155→| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\\\\n   156→| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\\\\n   157→| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\\\\n   158→| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\\\\n   159→| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\\\\n   160→| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\\\\n   161→\\\\n   162→**Checklist:**\\\\n   163→- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\\\\n   164→- [ ] Typography is readable\\\\n   165→- [ ] Information is logically organized\\\\n   166→- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\\\\n   167→- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\\\\n   168→\\\\n   169→---\\\\n   170→\\\\n   171→## Scoring Formula\\\\n   172→\\\\n   173→```\\\\n   174→Overall = (\\\\n   175→    Structure × 0.20 +\\\\n   176→    Characters × 0.25 +\\\\n   177→    Profiles × 0.15 +\\\\n   178→    Summaries × 0.20 +\\\\n   179→    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\\\\n   180→    Presentation × 0.10\\\\n   181→)\\\\n   182→```\\\\n   183→\\\\n   184→**Thresholds:**\\\\n   185→- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\\\\n   186→- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\\\\n   187→\\\\n   188→---\\\\n   189→\\\\n   190→## Issue Severity Classification\\\\n   191→\\\\n   192→When scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\\\\n   193→\\\\n   194→### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\\\\n   195→- Character merge/split errors for main characters\\\\n   196→- Missing major characters\\\\n   197→- Completely wrong chapter structure\\\\n   198→- Hallucinated content\\\\n   199→\\\\n   200→### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\\\\n   201→- Missing minor but named characters\\\\n   202→- Incorrect relationships for main characters\\\\n   203→- Multiple chapter summary errors\\\\n   204→- Major pronunciation gaps\\\\n   205→\\\\n   206→### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\\\\n   207→- Minor character description inaccuracies\\\\n   208→- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\\\\n   209→- Formatting/presentation issues\\\\n   210→- Missing some aliases\\\\n   211→\\\\n   212→### LOW (polish items)\\\\n   213→- Minor wording improvements\\\\n   214→- Edge case handling\\\\n   215→- Performance optimizations\\\\n   216→\\\\n   217→---\\\\n   218→\\\\n   219→## Evaluation Notes\\\\n   220→\\\\n   221→### Use Your Knowledge\\\\n   222→The evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\\\\n   223→- Verify character completeness against known casts\\\\n   224→- Check summary accuracy against known plots\\\\n   225→- Validate relationships and aliases\\\\n   226→\\\\n   227→### Be Specific\\\\n   228→Instead of: \\\\\\\"Character extraction has issues\\\\\\\"\\\\n   229→Write: \\\\\\\"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\\\\\\\"\\\\n   230→\\\\n   231→### Be Actionable\\\\n   232→Include file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\\\\n   233→- \\\\\\\"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n   234→- \\\\\\\"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\\\\\\\"\\\\n   235→\\\\n   236→### Focus on Threshold\\\\n   237→If score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\\\\n   238→\\\\n\\\\n<system-reminder>\\\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\\\n</system-reminder>\\\\n\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"aa5f2c10-d3e6-4a5e-b1a9-e6f755891dd5\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"a26d6d29-b7ce-4d47-b268-078bc52655a6\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/spec/output_quality.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\\\\n\\\\nThis rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\\\\n\\\\n## Scoring Overview\\\\n\\\\n| Category | Weight | Focus |\\\\n|----------|--------|-------|\\\\n| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\\\\n| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\\\\n| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\\\\n| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\\\\n| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\\\\n| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\\\\n\\\\n**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Category Details\\\\n\\\\n### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\\\\n- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\\\\n- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\\\\n- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\\\\n- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\\\\n- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\\\\n- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\\\\n- [ ] \\\\\\\"Chapter\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"Book\\\\\\\" vs \\\\\\\"Part\\\\\\\" hierarchy correct\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\\\\n- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\\\\n- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\\\\n- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\\\\n- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\\\\n- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\\\\n- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\\\\n- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\\\\n\\\\n**Common Issues:**\\\\n- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\\\\n- Full names and nicknames not linked\\\\n- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\\\\n- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\\\\n- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\\\\n- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\\\\n- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\\\\n- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\\\\n- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\\\\n- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\\\\n- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\\\\n- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\\\\n- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\\\\n- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\\\\n- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\\\\n- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\\\\n- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\\\\n- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\\\\n- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\\\\n- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\\\\n- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\\\\n\\\\n**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\\\\n\\\\n| Score | Criteria |\\\\n|-------|----------|\\\\n| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\\\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\\\\n| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\\\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\\\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\\\\n| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\\\\n\\\\n**Checklist:**\\\\n- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\\\\n- [ ] Typography is readable\\\\n- [ ] Information is logically organized\\\\n- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\\\\n- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Scoring Formula\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nOverall = (\\\\n    Structure × 0.20 +\\\\n    Characters × 0.25 +\\\\n    Profiles × 0.15 +\\\\n    Summaries × 0.20 +\\\\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\\\\n    Presentation × 0.10\\\\n)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Thresholds:**\\\\n- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\\\\n- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Issue Severity Classification\\\\n\\\\nWhen scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\\\\n\\\\n### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\\\\n- Character merge/split errors for main characters\\\\n- Missing major characters\\\\n- Completely wrong chapter structure\\\\n- Hallucinated content\\\\n\\\\n### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\\\\n- Missing minor but named characters\\\\n- Incorrect relationships for main characters\\\\n- Multiple chapter summary errors\\\\n- Major pronunciation gaps\\\\n\\\\n### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\\\\n- Minor character description inaccuracies\\\\n- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\\\\n- Formatting/presentation issues\\\\n- Missing some aliases\\\\n\\\\n### LOW (polish items)\\\\n- Minor wording improvements\\\\n- Edge case handling\\\\n- Performance optimizations\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Evaluation Notes\\\\n\\\\n### Use Your Knowledge\\\\nThe evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\\\\n- Verify character completeness against known casts\\\\n- Check summary accuracy against known plots\\\\n- Validate relationships and aliases\\\\n\\\\n### Be Specific\\\\nInstead of: \\\\\\\"Character extraction has issues\\\\\\\"\\\\nWrite: \\\\\\\"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### Be Actionable\\\\nInclude file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\\\\\\\"\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n### Focus on Threshold\\\\nIf score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":238,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":238}}}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01P5iFVQ9YZgWkJXk3pdd7oc\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"     1→# Oracle Loop Attempt 1 Summary\\\\n     2→\\\\n     3→**Purpose:** This document records what was tried during the first oracle loop run so future attempts can learn from these results and avoid repeating failed approaches.\\\\n     4→\\\\n     5→---\\\\n     6→\\\\n     7→## Executive Summary\\\\n     8→\\\\n     9→| Metric | Value |\\\\n    10→|--------|-------|\\\\n    11→| **Date Range** | January 17-18, 2026 |\\\\n    12→| **Total Iterations** | 31 |\\\\n    13→| **Texts Attempted** | Gatsby (5 attempts), Frankenstein (5 attempts) |\\\\n    14→| **Texts Passed** | 0 |\\\\n    15→| **Quality Threshold** | 8.0/10 |\\\\n    16→\\\\n    17→### Final Scores\\\\n    18→- **Gatsby:** 5.15 → **4.05** (WORSE by 1.1 points) ❌\\\\n    19→- **Frankenstein:** started at ~6.25 → **6.75** (minimal improvement) ❌\\\\n    20→\\\\n    21→### Key Finding\\\\n    22→The loop made Gatsby **significantly worse** and Frankenstein barely better. The fundamental issue is that **fixes kept causing regressions** in other areas, and there was no mechanism to detect or rollback these regressions.\\\\n    23→\\\\n    24→---\\\\n    25→\\\\n    26→## Results by Text\\\\n    27→\\\\n    28→### Gatsby (5 attempts, FAILED)\\\\n    29→\\\\n    30→| Attempt | Score | Commit | Fix Description | Outcome |\\\\n    31→|---------|-------|--------|-----------------|---------|\\\\n    32→| 1 | 5.15 | - | Baseline run | Chapter count wrong (7 instead of 9) |\\\\n    33→| 2 | 4.65 | `9bde9e5` | Prioritize hard boundary titles | ✓ Fixed chapters 7→9, ✗ Broke Wilson merge |\\\\n    34→| 3 | 4.65 | `9a29656` | Prevent family member merging | ✗ Created James Gatz/Gatsby split |\\\\n    35→| 4 | 4.65 | `31233a9` | Filter ambiguous last-name-only entries | ✗ ZERO impact |\\\\n    36→| 5 | 4.05 | Unknown | Unknown changes | ✗ Chapter count regressed 9→6 |\\\\n    37→\\\\n    38→**Critical Issues Never Resolved:**\\\\n    39→- James Gatz and Gatsby remained split (birth name vs known name)\\\\n    40→- Narrator identified as \\\\\\\"elevator boy\\\\\\\" instead of Nick Carraway\\\\n    41→- 626 pronunciation false positives\\\\n    42→\\\\n    43→### Frankenstein (5 attempts, FAILED)\\\\n    44→\\\\n    45→| Attempt | Score | Commit | Fix Description | Outcome |\\\\n    46→|---------|-------|--------|-----------------|---------|\\\\n    47→| 1 | N/A | `0d162f3` | CLI output path fix | ✓ SUCCESS |\\\\n    48→| 2 | ~6.25 | `4e3cf44` | Relational descriptor candidate pairing | ✓ PARTIAL - creature/monster merged |\\\\n    49→| 3 | 6.25 | `ba1215a` | Validation logic for relational merges | ✗ ZERO impact |\\\\n    50→| 4 | 6.25 | `432f7c1` | Diagnostic logging only | ✗ WASTED - no actual fixes |\\\\n    51→| 5 | 6.75 | `d501086` | Move relational pairing to execute first | ✗ ZERO impact |\\\\n    52→\\\\n    53→**Critical Issues Never Resolved:**\\\\n    54→- Alphonse Frankenstein fragmented into 5 entries (\\\\\\\"my father\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Father\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"M.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"M. Frankenstein\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Alphonse Frankenstein\\\\\\\")\\\\n    55→- William Frankenstein missing from character list\\\\n    56→- Henry Clerval split into 3 entries\\\\n    57→- 664 pronunciation false positives (~50% common English words)\\\\n    58→\\\\n    59→---\\\\n    60→\\\\n    61→## Approaches That FAILED (DO NOT RETRY)\\\\n    62→\\\\n    63→### 1. Filter ambiguous last-name-only entries\\\\n    64→**Commit:** `31233a9`\\\\n    65→**Rationale:** Remove single-word names like \\\\\\\"Wilson\\\\\\\" when both \\\\\\\"George Wilson\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Myrtle Wilson\\\\\\\" exist.\\\\n    66→**Result:** ZERO impact on character merging.\\\\n    67→**Why it failed:** The problem wasn't in candidate generation - the LLM was already rejecting merges.\\\\n    68→\\\\n    69→### 2. Block family member merges globally\\\\n    70→**Commit:** `9a29656`\\\\n    71→**Rationale:** Reject any merge where two names share a last name but have different first names.\\\\n    72→**Result:** Over-aggressive - caused James Gatz to be split from Gatsby.\\\\n    73→**Why it failed:** Too broad - blocked valid merges (birth names, aliases) along with invalid ones.\\\\n    74→\\\\n    75→```python\\\\n    76→# This logic was TOO AGGRESSIVE:\\\\n    77→if last1 == last2 and first1 != first2:\\\\n    78→    return False  # Different first names, same last = different people\\\\n    79→# Problem: \\\\\\\"James Gatz\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Jay Gatsby\\\\\\\" have different first names but ARE the same person\\\\n    80→```\\\\n    81→\\\\n    82→### 3. Adding diagnostic logging without implementing fixes\\\\n    83→**Commit:** `432f7c1`\\\\n    84→**Rationale:** Add logging to understand why merges weren't happening.\\\\n    85→**Result:** WASTED ATTEMPT - logging added but never analyzed or acted upon.\\\\n    86→**Lesson:** Don't commit diagnostic-only changes. Analyze, then fix, then commit.\\\\n    87→\\\\n    88→### 4. Moving relational pairing code position\\